# BioBlanks — PDP rebuild + Fourthwall headless

Handoff for continuing in Claude Code. Everything below is verified against
the live site and API unless marked otherwise.

---

## 1. What this project is

BioBlanks sells blank garments wholesale. The Webflow site is the marketing
and catalog layer; **Fourthwall** is the commerce backend for **sample orders
only**.

Two prices, two flows, never confuse them:

| | Price | Flow |
|---|---|---|
| **Sample** | $30.00 | Fourthwall cart → hosted checkout |
| **Wholesale** | $8.35 / unit | Typeform ("Start New Project"), no cart |

We are migrating off **Shopify + Shopyflow/Storesynk**, which has been
uninstalled. Its cart drawer was injected at runtime and is now gone —
a replacement has to be built in the Designer from scratch.

---

## 2. Architecture

Three tiers. Fourthwall's variant granularity (colour × size) is finer than
the image granularity (colour only) — that mismatch is why the Colorway tier
exists.

| Tier | Lives in | Count | Holds |
|---|---|---|---|
| Product | Webflow `Product Catalogs` | 22 | Spec, copy, traceability, SEO |
| Colorway | Webflow `Colorways` | ~66 | Image set, swatch, size→variant map |
| Variant | Fourthwall | ~400 | UUID, price, stock |

**The PDP makes zero Fourthwall calls to render.** Price and stock come from
the CMS at publish time; the Storefront API is only hit on add-to-cart.

Fourthwall's product model has **no metafields** and variant `attributes` is a
fixed shape — `color` (name + hex) and `size` (name), nothing else. All spec
data therefore stays in Webflow. This is a hard constraint, not a preference.

